WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:13.301
The Fair Labor Standards Act, a federal wage and hour law, requires Cisco to track all hours worked for the US non-exempt employees, including interns and part-time employees.

00:00:13.301 --> 00:00:17.365
Tracking time ensures compliance, and accurate overtime pay.

00:00:18.715 --> 00:00:28.379
Your status can change during your time at Cisco, for example when your job role changes, or when you move to a state whose laws are stricter than federal law.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:33.405
To check your own status, look at your offer letter.

00:00:33.405 --> 00:00:40.545
Or open Workday, go to your profile, choose Job, and on the Position tab, read FLSA Exemption Status.

00:00:40.545 --> 00:00:44.222
No, eligible for overtime, means you are non-exempt.

00:00:44.222 --> 00:00:47.969
Yes, not eligible for overtime, means you are exempt.

00:00:49.319 --> 00:00:55.271
This course is for US non-exempt employees who track their time, and for the leaders who manage them.
